Author: Trey OpenSpot <info@evqparking.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 1 22:32:07 2026 +0800

    Close run7 D50-D54: deterministic report primary, full evidence coverage, no denials, gated question channel, sanitized interpolation
    
    Independent verifier #7 (campaign verify-25af3b0) confirmed all eleven #66
    laundering shapes closed, then found the claim-rewrite path itself defective in
    five ways. All five are closed here; production stays on v92.
    
    D50 (P0) — evidence at 13 of ~30 mutating paths, false denials elsewhere.
    recordExecution is now wired at EVERY mutating path, per real id at the write
    site: person end/restore employment (genuine transition only), company field
    updates, permanent fixture deletes (company + cascaded people), channel and
    approval deletes, the deleteByIds family (product lines, specs, drawings, AI
    providers, MCP connectors, proposals), department/lead/document/product-line/
    spec/drawing/provider/proposal creates and updates, provider activation,
    company relationships, person assignments, memories, factory work orders.
    And the unsupported-claim correction no longer DENIES: "I can't confirm from
    this turn's execution record that X was ..." replaces "nothing was changed for
    it" — coverage is finite, so a denial can be false; only a CONTRADICTED state
    claim (disproven by the fresh canonical read) gets an assertive correction.
    
    D51 (P0) — the rewrite discarded the deterministic backend report.
    summaryIsFullyDeterministic/deterministicPrefix are computed above the
    structured-claim window from the function's own execution state; the rewrite
    now leads with the deterministic report and only appends claim lines. On a
    fully-deterministic turn (lifecycle report, org-graph check, plan confirm)
    only corrections are appended — supported claims would merely restate it.
    Real creates/updates/activations the model did NOT claim are reported
    directly from the evidence record (deletes already surface via factLines).
    
    D52 (P1, regression vs v92) — one supported claim disarmed the drift check.
    The rewrite now triggers on ANY mutation-shaped claim, not only rejections: a
    mutation turn's prose is re-rendered from verified structure every time, so a
    real create can no longer carry an unrelated fabricated completion. Read-only
    turns (no mutation claims, no rejections) remain untouched.
    
    D53 (P1) — questions[]/pendingAction were an ungated prose channel.
    safeProseFragment gates every question, proposedAction, pendingAction prompt
    and option label at construction (so the persisted envelope is clean too): a
    fragment asserting a past completion or carrying a uuid is dropped; genuine
    questions survive (Section R still proves prompt/options/questions render).
    
    D54 (P1) — three interpolations bypassed the F5 formatter.
    resourceType collapses to a word-shaped typed fallback (never raw), action
    renders only from the executor's own past-tense vocabulary (else "changed"),
    predicate must be a plain column name, and any value carrying a uuid renders
    as a neutral reference — closing the no-smuggling-required expectedValue leak.
    
    Test honesty (run7 scenario 9): F1/G previously asserted the D52 laundering
    shape as EXPECTED behaviour — both rewritten to the new contract in this same
    commit, with the change named. The lifecycle suite's Section X entries for
    D50-D54 flip from recorded-defect to fixed-contract per that suite's own
    two-way-drift discipline. New Section S asserts every recordExecution site at
    SOURCE level, because the windowed harness structurally cannot see those
    sites — the exact overstatement class run7 flagged; windowed X2 was NOT
    relabelled as covering them.
    
    Mutation-proven (byte-identical restore verified by sha256 after every case):
    removing the end_employment or lead-update evidence site, reverting the
    denial wording, dropping deterministicPrefix, disabling the question gate
    (via a UUID-FREE payload — X4's uuid-bearing payload masked this gate, found
    and fixed by mutation testing), interpolating action raw, rewriting only on
    rejections, and dropping the uuid value-scrub each fail the battery; all
    suites pass on restore. Full battery: structured_claim_verification 42/42,
    laundering 29/29 (DEPLOY GATE 0+0), lifecycle 75/75 + X 11/11 (0 open),
    issue5 binding, confirmation/restore/plan/person-lookup truth, past-completion
    regex, source-invariants drift guard all PASS.
    
    Still open, disclosed: D56 (read-only blanket replacement, parity with v92),
    D57 (#66 D45/D47/D48), historical_event unverifiable by construction (issue
    #5 A/C/D/E architecture). NOT deployed — production remains on v92; next step
    is independent verifier #8 against this commit, then the deploy gate.
    
